<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  RiverCrossing console: main_frame + main_menubar (spec.md 15b file map,
  xrc-windows.md section A). Control names are frozen; tests find them with
  FindWindowByName and tools/gen_ids.py turns them into ui/ids.py (R-05, R-73).

  Measured on wxPython 4.3.1 / wxWidgets 3.3.3 (tools/toolkit_probe.py):

    * wxInfoBar cannot be authored here. XRC yields a generic wx.Control and
      silently drops the name attribute, so FindWindowByName returns None.
      (This window carries none: the REOPENED corrections banner rides the
      status bar's first field, so nothing sits above the ride-info block
      and no code-side bar can disturb the frame's own sizing.)
    * wxDataViewListCtrl cannot be authored here either: its XRC handler
      hard-forces the control name to "dataviewCtrl". crossings_list and
      flagged_list are therefore wxDataViewCtrl, whose name IS honoured;
      columns, rows and per-row attributes are appended in code with a
      DataViewIndexListModel subclass (canvas code-side item 1).
    * wxMenuBar's XRC handler never applies the name attribute to the control
      (wxWidgets src/xrc/xh_menu.cpp). "main_menubar" is the resource id used
      by XmlResource.LoadMenuBar(); it does not resolve via FindWindowByName.
    * XRC has no minsize property for windows - only for sizeritem and
      wxSplitterWindow (wxWidgets src/xrc/xmlres.cpp SetupWindow). The
      canvas minimum of 1100x700 is declared as <size> below and must be
      re-applied code-side with SetMinSize(). (spec.md 13 says 1180x740;
      the canvas is implementation truth and wins - recorded conflict.
      W9 raises the declared size to 1100x780 code-side and here; the
      canvas drawing's own amendment is W15's. Phase 4 retires the
      30-row feed cap this height was sized around: crossings_list now
      scrolls the whole ride, and the pane height is a working area, not
      a row count. Phase 6 clamps whatever <size> or persisted geometry
      arrives to the current display's work area through
      _support.fit_frame_to_screen (wx.Display.GetClientArea, 16 px
      margin) and re-runs that fit on wx.EVT_DISPLAY_CHANGED, so a
      window saved on a larger or since-unplugged display still opens
      whole and on screen.)
    * Phase 6's Current Lap reading (current_lap_lbl) is a plain
      wxStaticText with a clock-sized relative font (the 64 DIP dial's
      own scale, spelled the way plate_input's 1.5x is) and its light
      green authored here with <fg>. Measured on this build (4.3.1 /
      wxWidgets 3.3.3, an XmlResource LoadFrame probe): the generic
      window handler DOES honour <fg>, unlike wxDataViewListCtrl's
      forced name or <relativesize> on a bitmap button. Only the
      two-digit width pin stays code-side - XRC cannot measure a font.

  Code-side per the canvas footnotes: feed columns/rows (with their
  header sort), bold flagged-row attributes, the feed's search filter,
  card bitmaps from the imagelist, main_splitter sash restore from
  settings, per-ride-state enabling of menus and buttons, radio
  menu-item defaults (see main_menubar below), and every data label's
  text.
-->
<resource>

  <object class="wxFrame" name="main_frame">
    <title>RiverCrossing</title>
    <size>1100,780</size>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <!--
        The ride-info block (plan §11: the stop light's status column,
        then the "Ride" and "Details" group boxes, then the ride logo
        slot), the two gauge-clock columns (WS-D) and the start/stop
        group. elapsed_clock_panel / remaining_clock_panel /
        ride_status_panel are code-side slots: XRC cannot author a
        wx.Control subclass, so RaceClock / StopLight (views/gauges.py)
        are built into these panels and named with SetName() in code
        (the code-side rule in the header above). The dials' numeric
        labels stay declared here under their frozen names
        (clock_elapsed_lbl / clock_remaining_lbl), and start_btn /
        stop_btn are wxBitmapButton shells whose SVG glyphs are set in
        code. XRC embeds no SVG and, measured, its bitmap-button
        handler ignores label text, so main_frame.py re-applies the
        labels there too.
      -->
      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>8</border>
        <object class="wxBoxSizer">
          <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <option>1</option>
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxBoxSizer">
              <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>

              <!--
                Plan §11: the ride-info block, left to right. The stop
                light's own column leads: Phase 6 wraps it in a native
                "Status" wxStaticBoxSizer so the group's fixed width is
                drawn, not implied: ride_status_panel is a code-side slot
                (the same XRC-cannot-author-a-wx.Control subclass rule as
                the two clock panels) holding the code-built StopLight
                (ride_status_light) beside its own label, whose width the
                view pins to the widest status word (ride_status_lbl,
                "REOPENED") so no state change can resize the column.
                Then two native group boxes replace the one "Ride"
                group. "Ride" carries the identity rows (Name, Date,
                Venue) and "Details" the organizer rows (Organizer,
                Scorer, Lap length km). Each row is an unnamed
                wxStaticText caption in column one and a wxTE_READONLY
                wxTextCtrl in column two, the counter chips' own caption
                convention; show_ride_header fills all six from the open
                ride's config. Both boxes carry label text only, no
                frozen name, so ids.py is unchanged (Phase 6's Status box
                is the same: the box title names it, no control does).
                The ride's own logo (ride_logo_bmp, rendered at 64x64)
                closes the block, to the right of both boxes and before
                the clock panels. It is authored with no bitmap element:
                measured on wxPython 4.3.1, XRC yields a real
                wxStaticBitmap that keeps its name and accepts SetBitmap
                later (about_logo_bmp's own authored shape).
              -->
              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
                <border>12</border>
                <object class="wxStaticBoxSizer">
                  <label>Status</label>
                  <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>
                  <object class="sizeritem">
                    <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
                    <object class="wxPanel" name="ride_status_panel">
                      <object class="wxBoxSizer">
                        <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>
                        <object class="sizeritem">
                          <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
                          <object class="wxStaticText" name="ride_status_lbl">
                            <label>DRAFT</label>
                          </object>
                        </object>
                      </object>
                    </object>
                  </object>
                </object>
              </object>

              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
                <border>8</border>
                <object class="wxStaticBoxSizer">
                  <label>Ride</label>
                  <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

                  <object class="sizeritem">
                    <object class="wxFlexGridSizer">
                      <cols>2</cols>
                      <vgap>6</vgap>
                      <hgap>6</hgap>

                      <object class="sizeritem">
                        <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
                        <object class="wxStaticText">
                          <label>Name</label>
                        </object>
                      </object>
                      <object class="sizeritem">
                        <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
                        <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="ride_name_value">
                          <style>wxTE_READONLY</style>
                          <size>240,-1</size>
                          <value></value>
                        </object>
                      </object>

                      <object class="sizeritem">
                        <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
                        <object class="wxStaticText">
                          <label>Date</label>
                        </object>
                      </object>
                      <object class="sizeritem">
                        <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
                        <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="ride_date_value">
                          <style>wxTE_READONLY</style>
                          <size>240,-1</size>
                          <value></value>
                        </object>
                      </object>

                      <object class="sizeritem">
                        <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
                        <object class="wxStaticText">
                          <label>Venue</label>
                        </object>
                      </object>
                      <object class="sizeritem">
                        <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
                        <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="ride_venue_value">
                          <style>wxTE_READONLY</style>
                          <size>240,-1</size>
                          <value></value>
                        </object>
                      </object>
                    </object>
                  </object>
                </object>
              </object>

              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
                <border>8</border>
                <object class="wxStaticBoxSizer">
                  <label>Details</label>
                  <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

                  <object class="sizeritem">
                    <object class="wxFlexGridSizer">
                      <cols>2</cols>
                      <vgap>6</vgap>
                      <hgap>6</hgap>

                      <object class="sizeritem">
                        <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
                        <object class="wxStaticText">
                          <label>Organizer</label>
                        </object>
                      </object>
                      <object class="sizeritem">
                        <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
                        <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="ride_organizer_value">
                          <style>wxTE_READONLY</style>
                          <size>240,-1</size>
                          <value></value>
                        </object>
                      </object>

                      <object class="sizeritem">
                        <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
                        <object class="wxStaticText">
                          <label>Scorer</label>
                        </object>
                      </object>
                      <object class="sizeritem">
                        <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
                        <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="ride_scorer_value">
                          <style>wxTE_READONLY</style>
                          <size>240,-1</size>
                          <value></value>
                        </object>
                      </object>

                      <object class="sizeritem">
                        <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
                        <object class="wxStaticText">
                          <label>Lap length km</label>
                        </object>
                      </object>
                      <object class="sizeritem">
                        <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
                        <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="ride_lap_km_value">
                          <style>wxTE_READONLY</style>
                          <size>240,-1</size>
                          <value></value>
                        </object>
                      </object>
                    </object>
                  </object>
                </object>
              </object>

              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxLEFT</flag>
                <border>8</border>
                <object class="wxStaticBitmap" name="ride_logo_bmp">
                  <size>64,64</size>
                </object>
              </object>
            </object>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>12</border>
            <object class="wxStaticBoxSizer">
              <label></label>
              <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>
              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxALIGN_CENTER_HORIZONTAL</flag>
                <object class="wxStaticText" name="current_lap_lbl">
                  <label>00</label>
                  <fg>#90EE90</fg>
                  <font>
                    <sysfont>wxSYS_DEFAULT_GUI_FONT</sysfont>
                    <relativesize>2</relativesize>
                  </font>
                </object>
              </object>
              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxALIGN_CENTER_HORIZONTAL</flag>
                <object class="wxStaticText">
                  <label>Current Lap</label>
                </object>
              </object>
            </object>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>12</border>
            <object class="wxBoxSizer">
              <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>

              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
                <border>8</border>
                <object class="wxPanel" name="elapsed_clock_panel">
                  <object class="wxBoxSizer">
                    <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>
                    <object class="sizeritem">
                      <flag>wxALIGN_CENTER_HORIZONTAL</flag>
                      <object class="wxStaticText">
                        <label>Elapsed</label>
                      </object>
                    </object>
                    <object class="sizeritem">
                      <flag>wxALIGN_CENTER_HORIZONTAL</flag>
                      <object class="wxStaticText" name="clock_elapsed_lbl">
                        <label>0:00:00</label>
                      </object>
                    </object>
                  </object>
                </object>
              </object>

              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
                <object class="wxPanel" name="remaining_clock_panel">
                  <object class="wxBoxSizer">
                    <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>
                    <object class="sizeritem">
                      <flag>wxALIGN_CENTER_HORIZONTAL</flag>
                      <object class="wxStaticText">
                        <label>Remaining</label>
                      </object>
                    </object>
                    <object class="sizeritem">
                      <flag>wxALIGN_CENTER_HORIZONTAL</flag>
                      <object class="wxStaticText" name="clock_remaining_lbl">
                        <label></label>
                      </object>
                    </object>
                  </object>
                </object>
              </object>

            </object>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxBoxSizer">
              <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>
              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxALIGN_RIGHT|wxBOTTOM</flag>
                <border>4</border>
                <object class="wxBitmapButton" name="start_btn">
                  <label>Start ride</label>
                </object>
              </object>
              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxALIGN_RIGHT</flag>
                <object class="wxBoxSizer">
                  <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>
                  <object class="sizeritem">
                    <object class="wxBitmapButton" name="stop_btn">
                      <label>Stop ride…</label>
                    </object>
                  </object>
                </object>
              </object>
            </object>
          </object>

        </object>
      </object>

      <!-- The plate entry row: the operator's whole working surface,
           framed by a native wxStaticBoxSizer as the console's find-me
           affordance (Phase 8 amendment; xrc-windows.md section A). -->
      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxBOTTOM</flag>
        <border>8</border>
        <object class="wxStaticBoxSizer">
          <label>Record crossing</label>
          <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>6</border>
            <object class="wxStaticText">
              <label>Plate</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>12</border>
            <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="plate_input">
              <style>wxTE_PROCESS_ENTER</style>
              <size>240,-1</size>
              <hint>Rider plate</hint>
              <font>
                <sysfont>wxSYS_DEFAULT_GUI_FONT</sysfont>
                <relativesize>1.5</relativesize>
              </font>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>12</border>
            <object class="wxButton" name="record_btn">
              <label>Record (Enter)</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <option>1</option>
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxStaticText" name="last_crossing_lbl">
              <label></label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxButton" name="undo_btn">
              <label>Undo last (Ctrl+Z)</label>
            </object>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

      <!--
        Crossings feed | review sidebar. The sash position is restored from
        settings in code (canvas code-side item 4); minsize keeps either pane
        from being dragged shut - the canvas draws the sidebar at 250 px.
      -->
      <object class="sizeritem">
        <option>1</option>
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxBOTTOM</flag>
        <border>8</border>
        <object class="wxSplitterWindow" name="main_splitter">
          <orientation>vertical</orientation>
          <minsize>200</minsize>

          <object class="wxPanel">
            <object class="wxBoxSizer">
              <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>
              <!-- Phase 4: the crossings search row, the rider editor's
                   own shape (riders.xrc: a wxStaticText label + a
                   wxSearchCtrl above the list). The label is the plain
                   word the editor uses and carries no frozen name, so
                   no ids.py entry rides on it. -->
              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxEXPAND|wxBOTTOM</flag>
                <border>8</border>
                <object class="wxBoxSizer">
                  <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>
                  <object class="sizeritem">
                    <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
                    <border>6</border>
                    <object class="wxStaticText">
                      <label>Search</label>
                    </object>
                  </object>
                  <object class="sizeritem">
                    <option>1</option>
                    <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
                    <object class="wxSearchCtrl" name="crossings_search"/>
                  </object>
                </object>
              </object>
              <object class="sizeritem">
                <option>1</option>
                <flag>wxEXPAND</flag>
                <object class="wxDataViewCtrl" name="crossings_list"/>
              </object>
            </object>
          </object>

          <object class="wxPanel">
            <object class="wxBoxSizer">
              <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

              <object class="sizeritem">
                <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxBOTTOM</flag>
                <border>8</border>
                <object class="wxFlexGridSizer">
                  <cols>2</cols>
                  <vgap>6</vgap>
                  <hgap>6</hgap>
                  <growablecols>0,1</growablecols>

                  <object class="sizeritem">
                    <flag>wxEXPAND</flag>
                    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
                      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>
                      <object class="sizeritem">
                        <object class="wxStaticText">
                          <label>Crossings</label>
                        </object>
                      </object>
                      <object class="sizeritem">
                        <object class="wxStaticText" name="crossings_count_lbl">
                          <label></label>
                        </object>
                      </object>
                    </object>
                  </object>

                  <object class="sizeritem">
                    <flag>wxEXPAND</flag>
                    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
                      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>
                      <object class="sizeritem">
                        <object class="wxStaticText">
                          <label>Cards dealt</label>
                        </object>
                      </object>
                      <object class="sizeritem">
                        <object class="wxStaticText" name="cards_count_lbl">
                          <label></label>
                        </object>
                      </object>
                    </object>
                  </object>

                  <object class="sizeritem">
                    <flag>wxEXPAND</flag>
                    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
                      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>
                      <object class="sizeritem">
                        <object class="wxStaticText">
                          <label>On course</label>
                        </object>
                      </object>
                      <object class="sizeritem">
                        <object class="wxStaticText" name="on_course_lbl">
                          <label></label>
                        </object>
                      </object>
                    </object>
                  </object>

                  <object class="sizeritem">
                    <flag>wxEXPAND</flag>
                    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
                      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>
                      <object class="sizeritem">
                        <object class="wxStaticText">
                          <label>Shoe</label>
                        </object>
                      </object>
                      <object class="sizeritem">
                        <object class="wxStaticText" name="shoe_lbl">
                          <label></label>
                        </object>
                      </object>
                    </object>
                  </object>

                  <!--
                    W12: the two registration chips (riders_count_lbl /
                    teams_count_lbl) appended after the four live-timing
                    chips. The roster counts are static per ride, so the
                    timing readouts stay topmost. The teams chip (its
                    caption and value) is hidden code-side in solo-only
                    rides (R-11); the caption carries no frozen name,
                    like every other chip caption, and is found
                    structurally by main_frame.set_team_ui_visible.
                  -->
                  <object class="sizeritem">
                    <flag>wxEXPAND</flag>
                    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
                      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>
                      <object class="sizeritem">
                        <object class="wxStaticText">
                          <label>Riders</label>
                        </object>
                      </object>
                      <object class="sizeritem">
                        <object class="wxStaticText" name="riders_count_lbl">
                          <label></label>
                        </object>
                      </object>
                    </object>
                  </object>

                  <object class="sizeritem">
                    <flag>wxEXPAND</flag>
                    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
                      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>
                      <object class="sizeritem">
                        <object class="wxStaticText">
                          <label>Teams</label>
                        </object>
                      </object>
                      <object class="sizeritem">
                        <object class="wxStaticText" name="teams_count_lbl">
                          <label></label>
                        </object>
                      </object>
                    </object>
                  </object>

                </object>
              </object>

              <!--
                Review notebook (WS-H): the roster on page 1 ("Riders",
                the default page, index 0), the flagged crossings on
                page 2 ("Needs Review", index 1). wxNotebook IS
                authorable here (measured on wxPython 4.3.1 /
                wxWidgets 3.3.3); the notebookpage node's own name
                attribute is dropped by the handler, so names live on
                the page children (the wxPanels) and the controls
                inside them. That is why
                flagged_list / review_btn / console_riders_list are
                declared where they are. Columns, rows, the
                double-click seam and the sorted header are code-side
                (main_frame.py); focus_review_panel finds the
                "Needs Review" page by its label, so a future reorder
                here cannot silently break it.
              -->
              <object class="sizeritem">
                <option>1</option>
                <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxBOTTOM</flag>
                <border>8</border>
                <object class="wxNotebook" name="review_notebook">
                  <object class="notebookpage">
                    <label>Riders</label>
                    <object class="wxPanel">
                      <object class="wxBoxSizer">
                        <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>
                        <object class="sizeritem">
                          <option>1</option>
                          <flag>wxEXPAND</flag>
                          <object class="wxDataViewCtrl" name="console_riders_list"/>
                        </object>
                      </object>
                    </object>
                  </object>
                  <object class="notebookpage">
                    <label>Needs Review</label>
                    <object class="wxPanel">
                      <object class="wxBoxSizer">
                        <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>
                        <object class="sizeritem">
                          <option>1</option>
                          <flag>wxEXPAND|wxBOTTOM</flag>
                          <border>6</border>
                          <object class="wxDataViewCtrl" name="flagged_list"/>
                        </object>
                        <object class="sizeritem">
                          <flag>wxALIGN_RIGHT</flag>
                          <object class="wxButton" name="review_btn">
                            <label>Review…</label>
                          </object>
                        </object>
                      </object>
                    </object>
                  </object>
                </object>
              </object>

            </object>
          </object>

        </object>
      </object>

    </object>

    <!-- Auto-attached to the frame by the XRC handler (SetStatusBar). -->
    <object class="wxStatusBar" name="main_statusbar">
      <fields>3</fields>
    </object>

  </object>

  <!--
    Seven menus, 48 mi_* items and three stock ids, mapping 1:1 onto the
    spec.md 15 table (File 8 - Ride 9 - Riders 5 - Cards 7 - Results 12 -
    View 1 row, 8 items - Help 4). File order follows the 15 table
    (Import CSV, Export CSV, Back Up, Simulation), not 15b's listing
    order.

    Results 12: mi_tiebreak_order retired; the tie-break order now comes
    only from the ride's stored config, set in Ride Setup. The single
    mi_preview_browser split into the per-format HTML/PDF preview
    items (Part D), each gated on its own export existing, and G6
    added the five checkable publish options after them (a separator
    first, since they are a second group), plus its rename of the
    HTML row to "Export HTML…". File 8:
    mi_simulation opens the Rider Simulator after Back Up Database.

    W14: mi_ride_setup left the Ride menu with its spec.md 15 row; the
    "edit this ride" setup semantics it implied were never built.

    D1/D2/D3 build them, on one surface: mi_new_ride moved off File
    into the Ride menu (which owns the whole ride lifecycle),
    mi_edit_ride opens the same ride_setup_dlg preloaded with the live
    ride's config, and mi_clear_ride (after a separator, being the
    menu's one destructive row) resets the open ride to a fresh
    DRAFT. D4 retires mi_add_entry from the Riders menu: the Rider
    Editor row is the single entry point for adding riders.

    Part D: mi_standings' "Enabled when" is now "always"; with no ride
    open the dialog's empty-state source covers it.

    wxID_PREFERENCES / wxID_EXIT / wxID_ABOUT carry no <label>: the stock id
    supplies the platform-correct text and lets wx relocate them into the
    macOS application menu (CODINGSTANDARDS-UX-DESKTOP.md section 5).

    Radio menu items get no <checked> here: wxWidgets' XRC handler applies
    that property only when kind == wxITEM_CHECK (src/xrc/xh_menu.cpp), so it
    is a silent no-op on wxITEM_RADIO. Code checks mi_zoom_100 - the one
    documented zoom default - after LoadMenuBar (W13: the theme trio left
    the View menu; the Settings appearance radios own appearance).
  -->
  <object class="wxMenuBar" name="main_menubar">

    <object class="wxMenu">
      <label>&amp;File</label>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_open_library">
        <label>Ride &amp;Library</label>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_duplicate_ride">
        <label>&amp;Duplicate Ride…</label>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_import_csv">
        <label>&amp;Import Riders CSV…</label>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_export_csv">
        <label>&amp;Export Riders CSV…</label>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_backup_now">
        <label>&amp;Back Up Database…</label>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_simulation">
        <label>&amp;Simulation…</label>
      </object>
      <object class="separator"/>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="wxID_PREFERENCES"/>
      <object class="separator"/>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="wxID_EXIT"/>
    </object>

    <object class="wxMenu">
      <label>&amp;Ride</label>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_new_ride">
        <label>&amp;New Ride…</label>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_edit_ride">
        <label>&amp;Edit Ride…</label>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_start_ride">
        <label>&amp;Start Ride</label>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_stop_ride">
        <label>Sto&amp;p Ride…</label>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_set_start_time">
        <label>Set Start &amp;Time…</label>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_finish_ride">
        <label>&amp;Finish Ride…</label>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_reopen_ride">
        <label>&amp;Reopen Ride</label>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_audit_trail">
        <label>&amp;Audit Trail…</label>
      </object>
      <object class="separator"/>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_clear_ride">
        <label>&amp;Clear Ride…</label>
      </object>
    </object>

    <object class="wxMenu">
      <label>Ri&amp;ders</label>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_rider_editor">
        <label>Rider &amp;Editor</label>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_team_editor">
        <label>&amp;Teams Editor</label>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_check_rider_issues">
        <label>Check for Rider &amp;Issues…</label>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_mark_dnf">
        <label>&amp;Mark DNF…</label>
      </object>
    </object>

    <object class="wxMenu">
      <label>&amp;Cards</label>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_undo_crossing">
        <label>&amp;Undo Last Crossing</label>
        <accel>Ctrl+Z</accel>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_add_crossing_at">
        <label>&amp;Add Crossing at Time…</label>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_edit_crossing">
        <label>&amp;Edit Crossing…</label>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_deal_manual">
        <label>&amp;Deal Bonus Card…</label>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_review_held">
        <label>Review &amp;Held Cards</label>
      </object>
    </object>

    <object class="wxMenu">
      <label>Re&amp;sults</label>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_standings">
        <label>&amp;Standings</label>
        <accel>F5</accel>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_export_html">
        <label>Export &amp;HTML…</label>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_export_pdf">
        <label>Export &amp;PDF…</label>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_export_poster">
        <label>Podium P&amp;oster PDF…</label>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_export_results_csv">
        <label>Export Standings &amp;CSV…</label>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_preview_html_browser">
        <label>Preview HTML in &amp;Browser</label>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_preview_pdf_browser">
        <label>Preview P&amp;DF in Browser</label>
      </object>
      <!--
        G6: the five publish options moved here from the results
        dialog's removed "Publish options" box. They are checkable
        (no <checked>: a check item's state comes from the persisted
        AppSettings.publish_* flags at startup, applied by
        app._check_loaded_publish_options). R-63's gate rides on the
        pair: with show times off, mi_time_board is unchecked and
        disabled (app._apply_publish_gate).
      -->
      <object class="separator"/>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_show_times">
        <label>Show lap &amp;&amp; total times</label>
        <checkable>1</checkable>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_laps_board">
        <label>Laps leaderboard</label>
        <checkable>1</checkable>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_time_board">
        <label>Fastest-time leaderboard</label>
        <checkable>1</checkable>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_full_field">
        <label>Full field</label>
        <checkable>1</checkable>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_all_cards">
        <label>All cards drawn</label>
        <checkable>1</checkable>
      </object>
    </object>

    <!--
      W13: the theme trio left this menu (the Settings appearance radios
      are the single theme surface). R-37's two independent time-column
      check items lead the menu: the Total column and the Lap time
      column, each mirrored by its own Settings checkbox. The zoom
      ladder is one radio group; wx groups consecutive wxITEM_RADIO
      entries, and the two checkable items between the menu's start and
      the ladder keep the zoom group from ever merging with a
      neighbouring radio item. The zoom items carry no mnemonic: seven
      numeric labels cannot hold unique ones, and the whole ladder is
      reachable with Alt+V then the arrow keys.
    -->
    <object class="wxMenu">
      <label>&amp;View</label>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_show_total_times">
        <label>&amp;Show Total Times on Crossings Panel</label>
        <checkable>1</checkable>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_show_lap_time">
        <label>&amp;Show Lap Time in Crossings Panel</label>
        <checkable>1</checkable>
      </object>
      <object class="separator"/>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_zoom_90">
        <label>Zoom 90%</label>
        <radio>1</radio>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_zoom_100">
        <label>Zoom 100%</label>
        <radio>1</radio>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_zoom_110">
        <label>Zoom 110%</label>
        <radio>1</radio>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_zoom_120">
        <label>Zoom 120%</label>
        <radio>1</radio>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_zoom_130">
        <label>Zoom 130%</label>
        <radio>1</radio>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_zoom_140">
        <label>Zoom 140%</label>
        <radio>1</radio>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_zoom_150">
        <label>Zoom 150%</label>
        <radio>1</radio>
      </object>
    </object>

    <object class="wxMenu">
      <label>&amp;Help</label>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_user_guide">
        <label>&amp;User Guide</label>
        <accel>F1</accel>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_shortcuts">
        <label>&amp;Keyboard Shortcuts</label>
      </object>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="mi_selftest">
        <label>Run Evaluator &amp;Self-test</label>
      </object>
      <object class="separator"/>
      <object class="wxMenuItem" name="wxID_ABOUT"/>
    </object>

  </object>

</resource>
